  "text": "**Solution 1 (answer 4) is wrong.** It asserts that a nonabelian automorphism group must be D_3 and that every twist has at most 4 rational preperiodic points. Both claims are unsupported. Quadratic rational maps admit larger automorphism groups (dihedral groups of several orders, and A_4), so restricting to D_3 is not justified. The bound of 4 comes from an unproven claim about torsion on the unit circle, not from a classification.\n\n**Solution 2 (answer 10) is more plausible.** It cites a classification of quadratic rational maps over Q with nonabelian automorphism groups, which I recall as the work of Yap and Doyle. I believe the maximum for that setting is 10, attained by a map with a tetrahedral (A_4) automorphism group, but I could not verify the citation or the count here. Its stated list of groups (D_3, D_4, D_6, A_4) is also not something I can confirm. My confidence is moderate, and the answer rests on recall of the literature rather than on a derivation I could check.\n\nCHOICE: 2",
